/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - An ideal solution is a model for a liquid mixture in which the chemical potential of every component follows one simple equation.
   - μi is the chemical potential of component i in the solution (J/mol); μipure is its chemical potential as a pure liquid at the same T and P; R = 8.314 J mol⁻¹ K⁻¹; T is temperature in K; xi is its mole fraction.
   - The standard state μipure is the pure liquid at the same T and P, not at 1 bar and not the ideal gas.
   - Lewis and Randall extended the pure-component fugacity to mixtures.
   - Real liquid mixtures disobey the rule.
*/
