/* book exam traps: ΔMmix includes the ideal part; ME does not. Do not set ME = ΔMmix for S or G; that is true only for H, U and V. | Excess properties are per mole of mixture. Multiply by total moles for a vessel; do not add a per-mole value to a total mole value. | ME = ΔMmix − ΔMmixid. Reversing the subtraction gives the wrong sign; a negative VE means contraction. | For ideal solutions ΔHmix and ΔVmix are zero, but ΔSmix and ΔGmix are not zero. Examiners often ask which ideal mixing changes vanish. | Activity coefficients come from the partial molar excess Gibbs energy, (∂(nGE)/∂ni), not from GE by a simple division. */
